---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import NavBar from '../components/NavBar.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Install" description="Install amber on Linux — from source in minutes">
  <NavBar />
  <main>
    <h1>Install</h1>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Dependencies</h2>
      <p>amber requires a C++17 compiler and a few development libraries:</p>
      <div class="terminal">
        <pre># Debian / Ubuntu
sudo apt install build-essential libcurl4-openssl-dev libncurses-dev

# Arch Linux
sudo pacman -S base-devel curl ncurses

# Fedora
sudo dnf install gcc-c++ libcurl-devel ncurses-devel</pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Build & Run</h2>
      <div class="terminal">
        <pre>git clone https://github.com/trefon/amber
cd amber
make

# Run the TUI
./amber

# Run headless
./amber-cli

# Run benchmarks
./amber-bench run --profile qwopus-27b</pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Configuration</h2>
      <p>amber reads from <code>amber.conf</code> in the project root and <code>~/.config/amber/</code> for global settings:</p>
      <div class="terminal">
        <pre># amber.conf (project-local — only data paths)
system_prompt=prompts/system.md
tools_prompt=prompts/tools.md
git_prompt=prompts/git.md

# Provider config lives in ~/.config/amber/providers/
# Example: ~/.config/amber/providers/llama.conf
api_base=http://localhost:8080/v1
model=Qwopus-27B-Fusion</pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>What Happens Next</h2>
      <p>When you run <code>./amber</code>, you'll see the welcome screen, the command drawer, and the slash command system:</p>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><code>/set model</code> — switch models at runtime</li>
        <li><code>/get model list</code> — list available models</li>
        <li><code>/set provider</code> — switch provider configurations</li>
        <li><code>/set detection namespace</code> — toggle loop/duplicate detection</li>
        <li><code>/compress</code> — force compression of conversation history</li>
        <li><code>/set policy</code> — configure approval rules</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Build System</h2>
      <p>amber uses a standard <code>configure</code> + <code>make</code> build system. The <code>GNUmakefile</code> auto-runs <code>./configure</code> to generate <code>Makefile</code> from <code>Makefile.in</code>:</p>
      <div class="terminal">
        <pre>make          # build everything (lib + cli + tui)
make test     # run unit tests
make lint     # run clang-tidy
make analyze  # run cppcheck
make clean    # remove .o / .d / binaries
make distclean # also removes the generated Makefile</pre>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
